{%- comment -%}
  Placeholder for a section that loads on demand (homepage sections below the fold).

  Why: the homepage HTML was ~185 KB compressed. On PageSpeed's slow-4G mobile test the whole document must
  download before first paint, and ~42% of it was sections nobody sees until they scroll. Those sections now
  render this skeleton instead. Their real HTML comes from Shopify's Section Rendering API
  (`?section_id=`) and replaces the skeleton:
    - right away if the placeholder is on screen (very tall screens, Googlebot's tall rendering viewport),
    - otherwise when the visitor first scrolls/touches/clicks and the section is within 1200px.
  The HTML is prefetched once the page has finished loading, so it's usually ready before anyone gets there.

  How a section opts in (sections/balad-*.liquid):
    {%- if section.index > 2 and request.design_mode == false -%} render this {%- else -%} real markup {%- endif -%}
  `section.index` is blank when Shopify renders the section through the Section Rendering API, so the fetch
  always gets the real markup.

  Accepts:
  - section_id {string} - section.id
  - kind {string} - 'cards' (product row skeleton) or 'block' (plain block). Default 'block'
  - h {number} - height in px on phones (<750px), measured from the real section
  - ht {number} - height on tablets (750-1199px)
  - hd {number} - height on desktop (>=1200px)

  Styles: end of assets/base.css. Loader: assets/lazy-sections.js (added by layout/theme.liquid when the page has placeholders).
{%- endcomment -%}
<div
  class="lazy-section lazy-section--{{ kind | default: 'block' }}"
  data-lazy-section="{{ section_id }}"
  style="--ls-h: {{ h | default: 500 }}px; --ls-ht: {{ ht | default: h | default: 500 }}px; --ls-hd: {{ hd | default: ht | default: h | default: 500 }}px;"
  aria-busy="true"
>
  <div class="lazy-section__inner" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="lazy-section__title"></div>
    {%- if kind == 'cards' -%}
      <div class="lazy-section__row">
        {%- for i in (1..4) -%}<div class="lazy-section__card"></div>{%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    {%- else -%}
      <div class="lazy-section__block"></div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>


